title: One presence per decision (TD-514), session env from the OS, PATH from signed config with tool dirs write-denied
summary: |-
  The founder's dogfood found that one mod install cost 4 passwords. TD-2026-10-20-514 makes every card decision cost exactly one presence: a helper 1.8.0 decision.sign op runs one LAContext over both the approvals key and the root key, and the kernel prepares every root row before the prompt. Aegis conditions C1-C7 are in: rootRows on the card, decision row v2 with rowsDigest, a helper-composed dialog line, a closed per-cardKind table, a cross-process grants lock and closure rule, and GUI fail-closed. Uninstall, voice.enrol (now root class), mcp.config, api-token and client decisionSig all cost 1. The founder signed the helper and the on-device probe passed twice.

  A second dogfood failure: sessions were refused with not_subscription_auth after the daemon self-upgraded. The re-exec env had dropped USER, and Claude Code finds its keychain login by $USER. The fix takes USER, LOGNAME, SHELL, TMPDIR and HOME from the OS. Session PATH now comes from config.sessions.path or a fixed default (TD-2026-10-21-077). Every user-writable PATH dir, including the whole Homebrew prefix, is write-denied for sessions (TD-2026-10-21-162; a brew-via-card flow is T-2026-10-21-005).

  Agent turn limits were raised to 100 on main (plugin 7.15.1, pushed bb93992b).
symbols_touched:
